# Diagram Template

```eraser
flowchart
    direction: top-down
    
    Start([Start]) --> Process[Process Step]
    Process --> Decision{Decision?}
    Decision -->|Yes| Success([Success])
    Decision -->|No| Error([Error])
    Success --> End([End])
    Error --> Process
    
    style Start fill:#e1f5fe
    style End fill:#e1f5fe
    style Success fill:#e8f5e8
    style Process fill:#f3e5f5
    style Decision fill:#fff3e0
    style Error fill:#ffebee
```

## Instructions

1. **Replace the title** with your diagram name
2. **Replace the Eraser code** with your diagram syntax
3. **Add comments** to explain complex parts
4. **Use styling** for better visualization (optional)
5. **Save as .eraserdiagram** file
6. **Open in VS Code** with Eraser extension

## Eraser Syntax Examples

### Flowchart
```eraser
flowchart
    direction: top-down
    A[Start] --> B{Decision}
    B -->|Yes| C[Action 1]
    B -->|No| D[Action 2]
```

### Sequence Diagram
```eraser
sequence
    participant A as Actor
    participant B as System
    A->B: Request
    B-->>A: Response
```

### Entity Relationship
```eraser
er
    ENTITY {
        id: int PK
        name: string
    }
```

### Architecture Diagram
```eraser
flowchart
    direction: left-right
    subgraph "Layer 1"
        A[Component A]
        B[Component B]
    end
    subgraph "Layer 2"
        C[Component C]
        D[Component D]
    end
    A --> C
    B --> D
```

## Styling Options

```eraser
style ComponentName fill:#color
```

Available colors:
- `#e1f5fe` (light blue)
- `#f3e5f5` (light purple)
- `#e8f5e8` (light green)
- `#fff3e0` (light orange)
- `#ffebee` (light red)
- `#e0f2f1` (light teal)
- `#fafafa` (light gray)